1
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:14,660
We often confuse loneliness with being alone.

2
00:00:15,540 --> 00:00:18,020
There is a vast, silent gulf between the two.

3
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:20,180
To be alone is a state.

4
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:23,240
To be lonely is a condition of the heart.

5
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:26,760
It is the sharp, quiet ache of feeling unseen,

6
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:30,620
felt not in the noise of a crowd, but in the stillness

7
00:00:30,620 --> 00:00:33,200
of a room where the walls seem to press in.

8
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:35,720
It is not just the lack of people.

9
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:37,980
It is the lack of connection.

10
00:00:38,820 --> 00:00:41,060
A person can be surrounded by hundreds and feel

11
00:00:41,060 --> 00:00:41,960
utterly invisible.

12
00:00:50,814 --> 00:00:51,794
Psychologist C.

13
00:00:51,794 --> 00:00:52,394
R.

14
00:00:53,154 --> 00:00:54,914
Rogers spoke of the conditions for growth.

15
00:00:55,774 --> 00:00:58,354
He believed that genuine empathy, unconditional

16
00:00:58,354 --> 00:01:01,854
positive regard, and congruence are the soil in

17
00:01:01,854 --> 00:01:03,234
which a person can thrive.

18
00:01:04,014 --> 00:01:05,614
Without them, we prune ourselves.

19
00:01:06,474 --> 00:01:08,314
We stop sharing our true thoughts.

20
00:01:09,094 --> 00:01:09,694
We wear masks.

21
00:01:10,574 --> 00:01:12,854
We become actors in a play where no one is watching,

22
00:01:13,614 --> 00:01:16,254
yet we feel the gaze of a judgment we cannot name.

23
00:01:16,254 --> 00:01:19,074
This is the social isolation that lives inside

24
00:01:19,074 --> 00:01:19,894
a busy house.

25
00:01:19,894 --> 00:01:23,234
It is the silence that speaks louder than the laughter

26
00:01:23,234 --> 00:01:23,834
of a party.

27
00:01:26,092 --> 00:01:27,132
Consider the modern condition.

28
00:01:28,052 --> 00:01:30,712
We are more connected than any generation in history.

29
00:01:31,512 --> 00:01:34,412
We send pings and packets, share images and status

30
00:01:34,412 --> 00:01:35,012
updates.

31
00:01:35,532 --> 00:01:37,312
Yet, the feeling of isolation persists.

32
00:01:38,372 --> 00:01:40,352
It may be that the speed of our connection has

33
00:01:40,352 --> 00:01:42,052
outpaced the depth of our understanding.

34
00:01:42,952 --> 00:01:45,052
We skim the surface of each other's lives.

35
00:01:46,032 --> 00:01:46,652
We perform availability.

36
00:01:47,852 --> 00:01:50,372
And in that performance, the core self retreats,

37
00:01:50,632 --> 00:01:52,352
hiding from the cold wind of indifference.

38
00:01:53,312 --> 00:01:56,072
We are lonely not because we are alone, but because

39
00:01:56,072 --> 00:01:56,672
we are not known.

40
00:02:06,445 --> 00:02:08,145
There is a philosophical shadow here.

41
00:02:08,845 --> 00:02:11,525
When we lose our sense of meaning, loneliness becomes

42
00:02:11,525 --> 00:02:12,445
more than social.

43
00:02:13,245 --> 00:02:14,265
It becomes existential.

44
00:02:15,465 --> 00:02:18,905
Albert Camus described the absurdity of a universe

45
00:02:18,905 --> 00:02:20,605
that does not speak back.

46
00:02:21,305 --> 00:02:24,145
If the world is silent, and we are alone with that

47
00:02:24,685 --> 00:02:26,925
silence, the weight of it is crushing.

48
00:02:26,925 --> 00:02:29,845
We push the boulder of daily life up the hill of

49
00:02:31,045 --> 00:02:31,645
expectation.

50
00:02:31,245 --> 00:02:32,785
It rolls back.

51
00:02:32,785 --> 00:02:33,505
We push again.

52
00:02:33,945 --> 00:02:36,105
The loneliness of the absurd is the loneliness

53
00:02:36,105 --> 00:02:37,905
of a question that has no answer.

54
00:02:38,685 --> 00:02:41,705
It is the echo of our own voice in a canyon with

55
00:02:41,705 --> 00:02:42,565
no other sound.

56
00:02:54,419 --> 00:02:55,819
But there is a turn.

57
00:02:56,599 --> 00:02:58,519
Loneliness is not a signal of failure.

58
00:02:59,359 --> 00:03:00,719
It is a signal of need.

59
00:03:01,679 --> 00:03:03,819
It is the body’s way of saying that the current

60
00:03:03,819 --> 00:03:05,279
arrangement is not enough.

61
00:03:06,059 --> 00:03:06,999
It demands attention.

62
00:03:07,899 --> 00:03:10,299
It asks us to look at the quality of our presence.

63
00:03:11,099 --> 00:03:12,979
Are we present when we are with others?

64
00:03:13,879 --> 00:03:16,719
Or are we already planning the next task, the next

65
00:03:16,719 --> 00:03:18,259
scroll, the next escape?

66
00:03:18,859 --> 00:03:21,779
If we are absent in our company, we are absent

67
00:03:21,779 --> 00:03:22,679
in our solitude.

68
00:03:22,679 --> 00:03:24,619
The loneliness is a mirror.

69
00:03:24,619 --> 00:03:27,479
It shows us that we have not met ourselves.

70
00:03:29,948 --> 00:03:32,468
To move out of the fog, we must change what we

71
00:03:32,468 --> 00:03:33,068
seek.

72
00:03:32,608 --> 00:03:36,168
We often look for distraction to silence the ache.

73
00:03:36,168 --> 00:03:38,468
We fill the space with noise.

74
00:03:38,468 --> 00:03:41,128
But the ache requires presence.

75
00:03:41,128 --> 00:03:44,268
It requires us to sit with the discomfort.

76
00:03:44,268 --> 00:03:47,888
To look at the empty chair and ask, what do I feel

77
00:03:47,888 --> 00:03:49,468
when I am truly alone?

78
00:03:50,228 --> 00:03:52,128
To feel the texture of the quiet.

79
00:03:52,888 --> 00:03:55,808
To let the silence be a companion, not an enemy.

80
00:03:56,588 --> 00:03:58,108
This is not easy.

81
00:03:58,108 --> 00:04:00,688
It is the hardest work we do.

82
00:04:01,408 --> 00:04:04,028
It is the work of becoming honest with the self

83
00:04:04,028 --> 00:04:06,068
that has been waiting to be heard.

84
00:04:15,857 --> 00:04:18,277
When we can be alone without fleeing, we can be

85
00:04:18,277 --> 00:04:19,597
with others without hiding.

86
00:04:20,417 --> 00:04:22,857
The depth of our solitude becomes the depth of

87
00:04:22,857 --> 00:04:23,457
our connection.

88
00:04:24,237 --> 00:04:25,117
We stop performing.

89
00:04:25,917 --> 00:04:26,877
We start listening.

90
00:04:27,877 --> 00:04:30,637
We meet the other as a subject, not an object.

91
00:04:31,377 --> 00:04:33,337
We share the weight, not the mask.

92
00:04:34,197 --> 00:04:35,677
The loneliness does not vanish entirely.

93
00:04:36,317 --> 00:04:36,917
It transforms.

94
00:04:37,797 --> 00:04:40,937
It becomes a quiet space between two people, a

95
00:04:40,937 --> 00:04:43,057
shared silence that is rich with understanding.

96
00:04:43,057 --> 00:04:46,097
It is the space where true intimacy lives.

97
00:04:46,097 --> 00:04:48,617
It is not the absence of noise.

98
00:04:48,617 --> 00:04:50,937
It is the presence of truth.
